# review-of-stage-high: the obligation is not delivered, and the door is not why

**NO-GO.** The obligation is `agents/tasks/LJ-1-565/Probe565.agda::stage-high`.
It is not inhabited. No postulate stands in for it. `StageHigh` is
`[LJ-1.536]`'s type, imported and not restated
(`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/Probe536.agda:350-352`, imported at
`Probe565.agda:47`). The probe is green: exit 0, `runs/full-t2.out`, median
1.94 s and 607 MB over three cold runs (`runs/full-t1.out`, `runs/full-t2.out`,
`runs/full-t3.out`).

**THE BRIEF'S QUESTION IS ANSWERED AND THE ANSWER IS YES: THE DOOR IS PAID.**
W3 is green on the first run. `AtStage` applies at `[LJ-1.536]`'s formula with
both hypotheses fed, and it gives membership in the definable powerset of the
stage with both directions (`runs/W3.agda:68-83`, exit 0, `runs/w3-0.out`,
median 1.93 s). `[LJ-1.562]`'s finding reaches this site.

**AND THE STOP IS STILL A STOP, BECAUSE THE DOOR WAS NEVER THE ONLY REASON
`[LJ-1.536]` GAVE.** That task's own stop names a second reason at
`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/review-of-StageHigh.md:88-91`:

> **THE LIMIT DID NOT LEAVE.** ... the induction that pays `HierBelow` has one
> case the adjunction cannot reach, and that case is a limit ordinal.

and its report names a third at `agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/lj-1.536-report.md:220-231`,
the successor row that exhausts 8 GB.

## What blocks it, measured

**THE SUCCESSOR STEP IS THE NEAR WALL AND THE LIMIT IS THE FAR ONE.** Both are
in front of `StageHigh` and neither is the door.

`[LJ-1.536]` split the successor row into three factors in one file that then
exhausted the heap (`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/runs/Control536d.agda:135-148`,
`runs/ctld-0.time`). It isolated factor 1 and factor 3 and it never isolated
factor 2. This task isolated all three.

| factor | `[LJ-1.536]` | this task | file |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1, the step arithmetic (`Control536d.agda:135-136`) | 425.73 s alone | **0.69 s, cured** | `runs/Control565a.agda`, `runs/ctla-0.time` |
| 2, the sequence identity (`Control536d.agda:140-144`) | never isolated | **HEAP WALL, 8 GB, 234.95 s** | `runs/Control565e.agda`, `runs/ctle-0.out` |
| 3, the target type (`Control536d.agda:147-148`) | free | **free, 1.75 s** | `runs/Control565j.agda`, `runs/ctlj-0.out` |

Factor 2's twin, with the same spelling on both sides so that no step is asked
for, costs 1.71 s (`runs/Control565f.agda`, `runs/ctlf-0.out`). That is the
controlled pair.

**FOUR ROUTES TO THE SUCCESSOR STEP WERE BUILT AND ALL FOUR WALLED.** Every one
of them is in `runs/` with its measurement: through `[LJ-1.536]`'s `seq`
(`Control565d.agda`, `Control565e.agda`), through the chapter's uniqueness law
(`Control565g.agda`, `Control565l.agda`), through a fresh instantiation of that
task's engine in the other spelling (`Control565h.agda`, `Control565k.agda`,
`Control565m.agda`), and through that instantiation with the one row of it that
this task cured (`Control565u.agda`). Eleven runs report
`Heap exhausted; Current maximum heap size is 8589934592 bytes` and one was
killed at 10.86 GB (`runs/ctll-0.out`).

**AND THE MOVE THAT ANY INDUCTION ON AN ORDINAL NEEDS IS PRICED THE SAME WAY.**
`MoveAlong` (`Probe565.agda:234-236`) carries the obligation along an equation
`sucV δ ≡ γ`. Two independent forms of it walled: a path in `IsOrd` built with
`isProp→PathP` (`runs/Control565s.agda`, 278.51 s, 8 GB) and the chapter's
uniqueness law (`runs/Control565t.agda`, 238.81 s, 8 GB).

## What is delivered instead

Ten green rows, each measured alone, are in `Probe565.agda`. They are both
halves of the successor step (`out` at `:131-139`, `into` at `:142-151`), the
engine applied at this site with those two halves as hypotheses
(`:168-178`), and the whole ordinal split (`:192-206`), which is free.

**SO THE SUCCESSOR STEP IS ONE APPLICATION SHORT AND THE APPLICATION IS THE
WALL.** `runs/Control565p.agda` is the engine with the two directions as
hypotheses, 1.79 s. `runs/Control565q.agda` is `out`, 1.67 s.
`runs/Control565r.agda` is `into`, 1.67 s. `runs/Control565u.agda` feeds the
second and third to the first: 8 GB, 238.63 s.

## What this does not claim

**THIS TASK DID NOT REACH THE LIMIT CASE AND IT MEASURED NOTHING ABOUT IT.**
`[LJ-1.536]`'s statement that the limit needs a witness inside the carrier
(`agents/tasks/LJ-1-536/review-of-StageHigh.md:88-91`, and
`dev/literature/devlin-II5.md:222`) stands untouched by anything here. This
report does not confirm it and does not refute it, and it must not be read as a
second site for `[LJ-1.560]`'s question. **The near wall stopped the work first.**
